  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.27 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.46. FLUX.2 and FLUX 3 no longer lose the WebGPU device on slower GPUs in the browser (RX 590 in Chrome: FLUX.2 Klein 4 losses in 27 first runs on 5.8.26, 0 in 30 on this; FLUX 3 Klein 0 in 10). Every native model forward now ends a command buffer per layer / block in the browser (the FLUX.2 text encoder went to the GPU as one ~2.7 TFLOP command buffer), and GraphExecutor (ONNX models) submits by estimated work, not only every 64 nodes (GraphExecutor.SubmitWorkBudgetFlops, default 128 GFLOP), so a full-resolution VAE decode is no longer one long command buffer. No math change and no measurable time cost; nothing changes on the desktop backends.",
